Description: Windows NT 4.0-style desktop shell for labwc
 Daytona recreates the Windows NT 4.0 desktop on Wayland: a taskbar with
 Start button, Start menu, window buttons, notification area (tray icons,
 volume control, battery, input locale, network through
 nm-applet, and balloons) and clock, a desktop with NT
 wallpaper modes, and NT's Run, Shut Down (with Stand by and Hibernate),
 Taskbar Properties, Display Properties, Date/Time Properties and Sounds
 Properties dialogs, event sounds from the freedesktop sound theme,
 and a screen saver
 and NT's Workstation Locked screen through swayidle and Daytona's own
 locker. labwc provides the
 window management, configured with NT key bindings, window menu and theme;
 the package includes its own build of labwc 0.8.3 with a small patch that
 draws NT's raised 3D window frames, installed privately in
 /usr/libexec/daytona so it does not replace a system labwc.
 .
 The package also contains the "daytona" Qt 6 style, which gives other Qt 6
 Widgets applications the NT look, and daytona-themetool, which applies
 Windows 95/NT/Plus! .theme colour schemes to the shell, Qt and GTK 3
 applications and labwc. A "Daytona" session is installed for login managers.
 .
 Daytona is not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. Windows and
 Windows NT are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies.

Package: daytona-greeter
Architecture: any
