Recommends:
 systemd,
Description: Windows 98-style log on screen for greetd
 An optional graphical log on screen that matches the Daytona desktop: a
 Windows 98-style dialog asking for a user name and password on the desktop
 colour, with a Session... button to choose the desktop to start (Daytona or
 any other installed Wayland session) and a Shut Down... button. It
 remembers the last user and session, uses the system keyboard layout and
 shows every question and message PAM has, such as one-time codes.
 .
 It is a greeter for the greetd login manager, which does the PAM, logind
 and session work, so the log on screen never runs as root. Installing it
 changes nothing until greetd is set to use it and is the system's display
 manager; see /usr/share/doc/daytona-greeter/greeter.md.

Package: daytona-chicago95
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Chicago95 GTK theme, icons and cursors for Daytona
 Chicago95 is a Windows 95 look for GTK, with matching icon and cursor
 themes. Daytona uses its icons and cursors throughout and applies its GTK 3
 theme, in the current Daytona colour scheme, to GTK 3 applications.
 .
 This package contains the Chicago95 GTK 2/3 theme and the Chicago95 icon
 theme, as pinned by Daytona (system icons only: without icons that replace
 an application's own icon and without the Windows logo), and the "Daytona
 Cursors" cursor theme: the
 Chicago95 Standard cursors redrawn for each pointer scheme (standard, large
 and extra large) and screen scale.
